# Source Code (`src`)

The `src` directory contains the main source code of the **AutoLink RadioSense** ESP32 firmware.

All core application logic and system-specific implementations are developed and organized within this directory. The source code is structured hierarchically into modules and subsystems to improve maintainability, readability, testing, and future development.

The core sub folder must contain program code needed to access for the whole project, or else being resused by multile novelties.
Other code must reside within the relavnt novelty folder, when orgazining the code within the novelty folders, follow the relavent WBS.

The directory is organized according to the project's major research novelties and their associated subsystems. Common system-level functionality may also be maintained in a shared `core` section.

Typical subsystems may include:

* Beacon Management
* Neighbour Management
* Link Quality Assessment
* Multi-Hop Forwarding
* Routing and Relay Selection
* LoRa Communication
* GPS Management
* Other supporting system components

Each subsystem may contain its own `.cpp` implementation files and `.h` header files.

The `main.cpp` file serves as the primary entry point of the firmware and coordinates the initialization and execution of the different subsystems.

src
  |--Core (Common code)
  |  
  |--Multihop Routing & Relay 
  |  
  |--Route Aware Hazards Filtering
  |
  |--Hazard Memory Network
  |  
  |--Store Carry Forward
  